    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our premier offensive catalyst. With an elite efficiency score of 83.29, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 14% park factor boost and an advantageous matchup against Gordon, whose SP_xERA sits at 4.04. Furthermore, his status as a dual-threat weapon is amplified by the opposing battery\u2019s slow delivery, maximizing his stolen base potential in a category that remains our primary focus. Joining him at the top of the board is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Jackson Merrill** (73.23). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** thrives against Ure\u00f1a due to a favorable platoon environment and a high-leverage spot in the #3 hole, while **Jackson Merrill** is perfectly positioned to capitalize on a 10% SP skill bump, providing us with elite scoring potential across the heart of the order.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision today involved **Tommy White**, who sat on the bubble with a score of 37.33. While his raw metrics were competitive, the brutal matchup against deGrom\u2014a pitcher who severely suppresses scoring efficiency\u2014ultimately pushed **Tommy White** below our 40-point floor threshold. We are also monitoring **Henry Bolte** closely; despite starting, his score of 41.38 is heavily suppressed by a negative 19% SP skill adjustment against deGrom, making him our highest-risk start. Elsewhere, **Nasim Nunez** provides a sneaky, high-floor play (58.46) primarily driven by his speed profile against Gusto; the 88% stolen base probability against this battery makes him a critical asset for our roster strategy, even when batting at the bottom of the order. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Henry Bolte** and the overall difficulty of the deGrom assignment, but our primary focus remains on aggressive base-running and maximizing the platoon advantages held by **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks**.",
